---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from "../config";
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header title={SITE_TITLE} />
    <main>
      <h1>👋🏽 Hi friends, I'm Will.</h1>
      <p>
        I'm a developer experience engineer and advocate focused on building
        better tools, and I give talks on improving the developer experience
        (DX). Presently I'm building things independently, but looking for
        something new with a great team. Let's <a
          href="https://calendly.com/willklein">chat</a
        >!
      </p>
      <p>Here are some things I've worked on:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          I helped maintain <a href="https://github.com/Workday/canvas-kit"
            >Canvas Kit</a
          >, an open source design system library at Workday. I welcomed new
          contributors and made contributions successful, grew an internal
          developer community, and created widespread adoption by making our
          tools the easy path for thousands of developers.
        </li>
        <li>
          I've spoken at conferences
          <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JMqZgUNkqgk" target="_blank"
            >across the globe</a
          >. I spoke most recently at <a
            href="https://jsnation.us/"
            target="_blank">JSNation US</a
          > about browser DX across Safari, Firefox, and Edge.
        </li>
        <li>
          I published a <a
            href="https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/markdown-menu-for-github/jekgocfoijmbgcjejohdgmojaejofdpo?hl=en#:~:text=Markdown%20Menu%20for%20GitHub&text=Adds%20a%20navigation%20menu%20to,include%20a%20Table%20of%20Contents."
            target="_blank">browser extension</a
          > to add a table of contents to GitHub READMEs and Markdown files. Years
          later, GitHub would eventually <a
            href="https://twitter.com/willklein_/status/1375688038651596810"
            target="_blank">implement it themselves</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          I've grown the local developer community through monthly events. I
          previously organized <a
            href="https://reactdenver.com/"
            target="_blank">React Denver</a
          > for several years, <a
            href="https://denverscript.com/"
            target="_blank">DenverScript</a
          > and founded HartfordJS.
        </li>
        <li>
          I teach people how to write their own dev tools through talks,
          workshops, and a little website: <a
            href="https://astsareawesome.com/"
            target="_blank"
            >ASTsareAwesome.com
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          I encourage new speakers to give their first meetup or conference
          talk, through direct mentorship and by organizing local workshops as
          part of <a href="https://twitter.com/gdcfpday" target="_blank"
            >Global Diversity CFP Day</a
          >.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Teaching Developer Advocacy</h2>

      <p>
        If you're writing code or building a product that other developers use,
        you're doing developer relations. If you want to be more intentional
        than accidental, let's have a chat: <a
          href="https://calendly.com/willklein"
          >https://calendly.com/willklein</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        My recent background is in design systems, but I'm also a specialist
        in building developer tools and designing a better developer
        experience. This includes documentation, community building, and
        improving cross-team relationships.
      </p>
      <p>
        I gave a <a
          href="https://youtu.be/fxGkzGZFxVo?si=zjU3lLoAmOANDHih&t=33"
          >talk last September at CascadiaJS</a
        > that I hope will help you too.
      </p>

      <h2>Helping Friends Get Hired</h2>

      <p>
        If you're looking for a new role, check out the <a
          href="https://platform.torc.dev/#/r/JLcPkIFf/cp">Torc community</a
        >. I happen to be a Torc Ambassador – deservedly so – because they are
        a supportive bunch with lots of content around resumes & how to apply
        to roles effectively.
      </p>

      <p>
        Connect with me on <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/willklein"
          >LinkedIn</a
        > too, and send me a note/DM with what you're looking for. I'm always
        here to help whenever I can!
      </p>

      <Footer />
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
